# CM7 DAC / control-tick timing (mandatory)

## Confirmed cause (2026-07-17)

Calling `dac_ctrl` / `WriteMotorDAC` from **CM7** every Customer tick blocks on
`ICC_SendPacket_WITH_ID` + `ICC_WaitForResponse` (up to 1000 ms). Two channels per
tick made `GEO_ApplicationTask_Update` run at ~240–400 ms instead of ~5–10 ms.

Bench: DAC on → `[CM7 UPDATE]` ~2400–4000 ms / 10 calls; DAC commented → ~50 ms / 10 calls.

Full plan: `.cursor/Logs/Log18-CM7-DAC-ICC-blocking-tick-fix-plan.md`  
Timing table: `.cursor/Logs/Log15-System-Timing-Reference.md` §1.1

## Rule

- **Do not** put per-tick motor DAC updates on CM7 via `dac_ctrl` (blocking ICC).
- **Do** apply DAC on **CM4** (SPI owner); CM7 publishes right/left commands over
  Customer ICC NO_ID (same pattern as steering → Pololu).
- Temporary comment-out of `WriteMotorDAC` on CM7 is a diagnostic only — restore via Log18 Stage 1, not by re-enabling blocking CM7 `dac_ctrl` in the hot path.

## Current tree state (2026-07-20)

**Active:** `NewBoard/Rewrite/MFCB_BASE` — motor ICC **v2 µV**: CM7 scales, CM4 clamps +
local `dac_ctrl` (guideline — see `cm7-process-cm4-io-guideline.mdc`). Peek/RX age 300 ms.
